  "raw": {
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197125": {
      "title": "Lecturer In Midwifery - Internal Applicants Only",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Lecturer In Midwifery - Internal Applicants Only £41,064 rising to £44,746 pro rata Part Time, Fixed Term - Academic PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. We are looking for a motivated individual to join the Midwifery programme academic team at Oxford Brookes for the role of fixed term Lecturer (maternity cover) 0.5 FTE. We are a supportive team who are passionate about high quality midwifery pre-registration education, as evidenced by consistently strong performance in NSS and other national league tables. With close working relationships with practice partners this is an excellent opportunity for the right individual to be part of educating the midwives of the future. Qualifications required : Current NMC registration as a Registered Midwife; Bachelor's degree in Midwifery. Evidence of, or a willingness to undertake study at Master’s degree level and/or Doctoral level, and evidence of, or a willingness to work towards a teaching qualification or equivalent. Experience required for post : A clinical background in midwifery, including NIPE qualification. Experience in teaching/assessing at pre-registration undergraduate level. Evidence of supervising and educating students in practice. Evidence of successfully managing and completing projects in a practice or educational setting. Evidence of research and/or scholarly activity commensurate with the stage of career. Overall purpose of all posts : To deliver high quality education in midwifery to pre-registration students at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including students on the shortened programme who are already registered adult nurses; to supervise undergraduate and postgraduate projects; to participate in student recruitment; to support students in clinical placements and liaise with relevant stakeholders where appropriate. For informal enquiries about these posts please contact: Dr Jane Carpenter, Associate Professor and Programme Director of Midwifery; Lead Midwife for Education jane.carpenter@brookes.ac.uk Please note that this role will not attract sufficient points for skilled worker sponsorship. Provisional interview date is 27th October. Benefits Our employees' well-being, physical, mental and financial, is incredibly important to us. This is why we offer our employees a varied and comprehensive benefits package. As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy 35 days holiday, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). You will have access to the Teachers pension scheme, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities and access to a variety of other university facilities including NHS Dentist, Brookes on-site Nursery Discounted travel options (Discounted bus travel in and around Oxford, BrookesBus - Park & ride scheme, Interest-free loans for travel tickets and cycle to work scheme) TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme - £5000 for candidates moving more than 30 miles on a permanent basis. Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instill a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it. a vibrant and inclusive place to work Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. To send this role to a friend, please copy the following link: https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197125 Closing Date : 16-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197125 Faculty or Directorate : Health, Science and Technology Location : Marston Road Site, Oxford For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 29-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196965": {
      "title": "Access & Outreach Assistant",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Access & Outreach Assistant £28,778, rising to £31,236 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. About the Role Are you passionate about fair access to education and inspiring young people to achieve their potential? As our Access & Outreach Assistant , you will play a frontline role in helping Oxford Brookes University achieve its Access & Participation targets. Working within our Access Projects Team, you will deliver engaging information, advice, and guidance (IAG) workshops in schools and colleges, coordinate sustained access programmes for underrepresented students, and support the logistics behind our major campus events. What You Will Be Doing: Delivering Impact: Presenting interactive talks and workshops to young people across schools and colleges in the region. Project & Event Coordination: Supporting sustained widening access programmes and assisting with large-scale inbound events (booking venues, managing student ambassadors, and logistics). Data & Administration: Managing the school liaison inbox and inputting student/event data into HEAT (Higher Education Access Tracker) to evaluate our impact. Collaboration: Supporting academic staff with subject-specific outreach and contributing to major university events like Open Days and Clearing. What You Need: Awareness of the UK Higher Education student recruitment and Widening Participation (WP) context. Experience working with young people or delivering presentations/workshops to groups. Strong organizational, IT, and administrative skills. A Full UK Driving Licence and willingness to undertake extensive regional travel, along with occasional evening/weekend work. A degree OR equivalent professional experience in education, youth work, or community engagement. (Note: The successful candidate will require a DBS background check before appointment. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role). About the Location This is a hybrid role split between the Headington Campus and working from home, requiring 1–2 days on campus, remote working, and regional travel. Why Join Us? At Oxford Brookes University, our people are at the heart of everything we do. As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous Employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees - both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Membership to HELOA and NEON Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer, we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196965 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 196965 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment & Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 28-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197145": {
      "title": "Head of Development and Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Head of Development and Alumni Engagement £78,186, rising to £85,414 Full Time, Permanent - Senior Staff Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward-thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “We shape tomorrow through the open and inclusive exchange of knowledge and ideas” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role As the Head of Development and Alumni Engagement, you will report to the Director of Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement and lead the Development and Alumni Relations Team. You will be based at our Headington campus and lead the strategy for fundraising and alumni relations, build relationships with major donors, and expand our global alumni network. About the team The Development and Alumni Relations Team works to build strong, lifelong connections with Oxford Brookes alumni, supporters, and friends worldwide. The team is responsible for securing philanthropic support, managing donor stewardship, and delivering impactful alumni engagement programs to advance the University's strategic goals and support its vibrant community. What will I be doing? Lead and manage the Development and Alumni Relations Team to deliver ambitious fundraising and alumni engagement goals. Develop and execute a comprehensive fundraising strategy focusing on major gifts, individual giving, and corporate partnerships. Build and maintain relationships with high-net-worth individuals, key donors, alumni, and external stakeholders. Oversee alumni relations programs to increase engagement, volunteering, and lifelong connections with the University. Work closely with the Director of Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement and senior leadership to align initiatives with University priorities. What skills do I need? Proven track record of success in major gift fundraising and alumni engagement within higher education or the non-profit sector. Strong leadership and team management skills with a track record of motivating and developing staff. Exceptional communication, negotiation, and interpersonal skills to build effective relationships with diverse internal and external stakeholders. Strategic thinking and expertise in planning and executing successful fundraising campaigns. About the location Based at our Headington campus, you will experience a vibrant campus atmosphere in a modern office environment located close to Oxford city centre. Hybrid working arrangements are supported depending on operational requirements. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 30 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous Employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197145 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197145 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment & Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 30-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196245": {
      "title": "Student Mental Health & Welfare Support Practitioner",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Student Mental Health & Welfare Support Practitioner £41,064 rising to £44,746 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to, a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised university focused on providing high-quality teaching and delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new, and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze Award and a Race Equality Charter Bronze Award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Oxford Brookes University has a vacancy for a Student Mental Health and Welfare Support Practitioner. The team works on a hybrid model with both on campus and remote working required. About the team You will be part of a small team of Student Mental Health and Welfare Support Practitioners within the Student Mental Health and Welfare Support Service. What will I be doing? As a Student Mental Health and Welfare Support Practitioner, you will be responsible for: Providing a first and regular point of contact for vulnerable students, those at risk or in crisis, or with substantial and enduring mental health conditions, those who may be reluctant to access professional services, or students who are unsure of which support services to access. Providing streamlined assessments, identifying clear referral pathways (internal and external), and offering support and guidance to students who are having difficulties functioning or continuing their studies for non-academic reasons or who are eligible for reasonable adjustments to help them successfully engage with University life and avoid crises. Providing specialist advice, guidance and support to students (both prospective and current students ) who have disclosed mental health as a disability or who have mental health difficulties more generally, which may or may not be in addition to a disability. Providing advice and support to colleagues within Student Support Services and other University staff when dealing with critical student events. Respond to serious concerns about students, undertaking risk assessments of their situations, face-to-face (in-person or online video) or by telephone with students who are at risk of harm to themselves or others, engage in safety planning, conduct brief solution-focused interventions and signpost to appropriate internal and external agencies. Offer a practical, problem-solving, flexible approach to helping students successfully engage with their academic studies and appropriate support services. This may include meetings with students who must present themselves following disciplinary or other offences. What skills do I need? Student Mental Health and Welfare Support Practitioner skills and experience Qualification at degree level or equivalent in a relevant area (e.g. social work, mental health nursing, counselling or a similar related field). Experience in providing streamlined assessments, face to face (in person or via an online video platform or by telephone) to determine the nature and duration of help required by the individual, including identifying clear referral pathways (internal and external). Experience in assessing and managing risk of harm to self and others in a front-line provision. Experience working on a 1-to-1 basis with students/adults in distress, affected by mental health difficulties or with other complex and multi-dimensional needs. Experience in working as part of a multidisciplinary team in an organisational setting. Experience in providing culturally sensitive interventions in a multicultural environment. Excellent verbal and written communication skills and an ability to communicate complex information to others. Excellent interpersonal skills. Ability to stay calm under pressure and manage challenging behaviour. About the location Based at our Headington campus, you’ll experience the vibrant campus atmosphere and benefit in our modern office environment. The campus is one mile from the centre of Oxford and is served by regular public transport. This role will be hybrid and we expect the successful applicant to be onsite 4 days per week (until 5pm) with 1 day working from home. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes staff member, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 holidays and additional university concessionary days (normally 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government Pensions Scheme with generous employer contributions, as well as providing all staff with access to an occupational health service, financial education, and a comprehensive assistance helpline. We prioritise the wellbeing of our employees - physically, mentally and financially - and we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the university sports and gym facilities An on-site nursery (at Headington Campus; waiting lists for some ages). Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles, subject to terms of the scheme) Training and development opportunities A connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks, which instil a sense of community and offer employees a space for support, guidance and friendship, making Brookes a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196245 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 196245 Faculty or Directorate : Academic and Student Administration Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 23-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197325": {
      "title": "Student Support Coordinator - Internal Applicants only.",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/10/2026 Student Support Coordinator - Internal Applicants only. £36,636 rising to £39,906 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role We are looking to recruit two Student Support Coordinator posts. One role will be based for three days at Headington Campus, in the Student Hub, and one will be split between Marston and Headington Campus (Student Hub). Both posts report to the Senior Student Support Coordinator for the Faculty of Health, Science and Technology. Student Support Coordinators provide support, advice and guidance for students on a wide range of academic and pastoral issues in a confidential setting. Student Support Coordinators are a student’s first point of contact for wellbeing and programme advice in the Student Hub, acting as a triage point for a range of student support services available across the University. When not meeting with students, you will be required to manage your time effectively to undertake a range of administrative tasks including responding to emails and student contact forms, undertaking work under Support to Study, maintaining programme information and contributing to service development. Interviews are expected to take place on 4th or 5th November. As a Student Support Coordinator you will: Provide guidance, advice and support to students on a variety of subjects such as Exceptional Circumstances, our Student Systems and Virtual Learning Environment, University regulations and rules, module registration, course changes and others. Signpost and make direct referrals to other Student Support Services whenever appropriate. Maintain accurate Service Now records of student interactions, in line with training and templates provided. Collaborate on reports for evaluating the operation of Student Support Coordinator activities in order to identify trends and student demands. Respond to enquiries from students and staff on a wide range of subjects, through a variety of channels. You should have: Proven experience of delivering positive customer service to people who have complex and multi-dimensional needs. Experience of dealing with highly sensitive and confidential information within data protection legislation. The ability to maintain clear boundaries when working in a one-to-one situation. The ability to stay calm under pressure and handle difficult conversations and sometimes challenging behaviour. An undergraduate degree or substantial relevant work experience in a post with similar general support and advice duties. Proven administrative and computer skills in the provision and recording of information, advice and guidance services; through in-person interactions, in writing, via telephone, and via video-call systems such as Zoom. The ability to liaise with and build effective working relationships with people at all levels, including senior staff. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. The successful candidate will have proven experience of working with people at all levels, dealing with highly sensitive and confidential information, and delivering a positive customer-focused service. They will be skilled in the provision of advice and guidance services, with proven written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills. They will understand the importance of team working within this environment. About the location This will be a hybrid role requiring three days on campus per week. One role will be based for three days at Headington Campus (Student Hub), one will be split between Marston and Headington Campus (Student Hub). You’ll experience a vibrant campus atmosphere and benefit from our modern office in the Student Hub. The campus is one mile from the centre of Oxford and is served by regular public transport. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme , as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197325 Closing Date : 18-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197325 Faculty or Directorate : Academic and Student Administration Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.acuk Posted on : 02-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197485": {
      "title": "Procurement Buyer - Academic & Student Services, Digital & Technology and Professional & Business Services. - Internal Applicants only.",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Procurement Buyer - Academic & Student Services, Digital & Technology and Professional & Business Services. - Internal Applicants only. £29,354 rising to £31,861 Full Time, Fixed Term - Professional Ser PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. If you wish to apply as a secondment please speak to your line manager. Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward-thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Based at our Headington campus and reporting to the Senior Category Manager, the Procurement Buyer (Academic & Student Services, Digital & Technology and Professional & Business Services) will lead, undertake, and support end-to-end procurement and contract management activities. You will act as a primary contact for procurement queries, drive cashable savings, support supplier negotiations, and ensure full compliance and governance across key spend categories. This is a full time 6-month fixed-term post and is available immediately. About the team You will join the Procurement team within Finance and Legal Services as Oxford Brookes transforms how it spends £50 million annually on goods, services, and construction. The team collaborates closely with internal academic and operational stakeholders, as well as external suppliers and framework providers. Our ambition is to modernize procurement, deliver operational excellence, drive financial savings, and elevate the overall student and staff experience. What will I be doing? Leading and supporting quotes, tenders, and call-offs from Framework Agreements, including running e-tendering processes. Acting as the main point of contact for internal and external procurement queries, triaging requests, and building strong stakeholder relationships. Monitoring supplier performance and SLA/KPI compliance, organizing contract reviews via ServiceNow for Gold, Silver, and Bronze contracts. Conducting spend analysis and producing regular reporting, including weekly high-value spend and monthly purchasing card reports. Supporting price and service negotiations alongside Category Managers to hit organisational annual savings targets. Guiding internal University colleagues through tender evaluation and moderation processes. Facilitating the roll-out of procurement training and self-service resources to contract owners across the University. Deputising for Category Managers when required and representing the department at relevant professional events. What skills do I need? Excellent communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills in a professional environment. Strong operational, organisational, and problem-solving abilities with high attention to detail. Strong numeracy skills with the ability to analyse, manipulate, and present spend data logically. Self-motivated and adaptable approach, with proven ability to prioritise workloads and meet savings and compliance targets. Prior experience in procurement-related roles and working towards MCIPS (Desirable). Familiarity with e-procurement platforms, ServiceNow, or Higher Education finance systems (Desirable). Practical understanding of procurement governance, policies, and legislative compliance (Desirable). This role closes: Wednesday 21st October 2026 Interviews: w/c 2nd November 2026 Any queries regarding the role, please contact the recruiting manager, Kelly Michell (via macmailbox@brookes.ac.uk), for an informal conversation about this role. This role will not attract sufficient points to obtain a sponsored skilled worker visa under the points based immigration system, however applications are welcome from candidates who don’t currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a visa via another route . About the location Based at our Headington campus, you will experience a vibrant atmosphere and modern office environment just one mile from Oxford city centre, with excellent public transport links. This role operates on a hybrid working pattern, typically requiring a 50/50 split between home and campus working. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days' holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme as well as providing all staff with financial education and a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community, offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship, making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer, we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197485 Closing Date : 21-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197485 Faculty or Directorate : Finance and Legal Services Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 09-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196748": {
      "title": "Web and Digital Communications Manager",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Web and Digital Communications Manager £47,389, rising to £51,753 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgement of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow The role : Based at our Headington Campus (with hybrid working), you will report to the Deputy Head of Strategic Marketing and Communications – Marketing and Digital. You will oversee the delivery, governance, and management of the University’s main website, student portal, and staff intranet, while managing a team of digital specialists. About the team: The Strategic Marketing and Communications team sits within the Directorate of Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement, driving Oxford Brookes’ global profile, strategic student recruitment, and brand reputation. The team oversees digital channels, user experience, and content strategy, working with stakeholders across the University and external vendors. You will directly manage a team of five specialists covering web content, design accessibility, analytics, and digital experience projects. What will I be doing? Managing the University’s main website (Brookes.ac.uk), new Student Experience portal, and staff intranet. Leading a team of five web, digital, and user experience specialists. Stewarding the ongoing web transformation project and implementation of the Contensis content management system. Setting and upholding digital governance, quality assurance, brand standards, and WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility compliance. Managing vendor relationships, SLAs, third-party contracts, and the Customer and Channels budget (c. £200,000). Collaborating with Information Services on system security, data integration, and platform architecture. What skills do I need? Degree-level qualification or equivalent significant professional experience. Extensive experience managing large, complex websites and content management systems (ideally Contensis). Proven track record in digital project delivery, user experience (UX), and digital channel optimisation. Strong technical background in website architecture, accessibility standards (WCAG), and search/AI visibility. Strong leadership and line management skills, with experience managing vendor and stakeholder relationships. Excellent interpersonal and time-management skills. About the location: Based at our Headington Campus, you will enjoy a modern office setting just one mile from Oxford city centre with excellent public transport links. This post supports hybrid working, allowing a balance between home and campus-based work. Benefits: You will enjoy 25 days of annual leave (rising to 28 days with service), plus 8 Bank Holidays and approximately 5 University concessionary days per year. We offer a flexible hybrid working setup with provided equipment, alongside a highly competitive Local Government Pension Scheme. Additional perks include discounted gym access, an on-site nursery, travel discounts, TOTUM savings, training opportunities, and active staff support networks. We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work Equality, diversity and inclusion: At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer, we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. Timeline: The closing date for applications is 22 Oct 2026 https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196748 Closing Date : 22-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 196748 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment & Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 24-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197465": {
      "title": "Applicant & Enquiry Adviser",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Applicant & Enquiry Adviser £28,778, rising to £31,236 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to, a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised university focused on providing high-quality teaching and delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new, and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze Award and a Race Equality Charter Bronze Award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The Role Based at our Headington Campus and reporting to the Senior Applicant Engagement Officer, the Applicant & Enquiry Adviser plays a vital role in delivering a high-quality experience for prospective students and applicants. As part of the Marketing and Communications Directorate, you will act as a named contact, providing personalised advice and support, responding to enquiries across channels including The Student Room, Unibuddy, phone, and CRM systems, and contributing to student recruitment objectives. Working within the Applicant Engagement team, you will help ensure all applicants receive timely, accurate, and professional responses, support campaigns and events, and contribute to targeted conversion activity across key UK and international markets, ensuring every interaction with Oxford Brookes is positive and engaging. What will I be doing? Responding efficiently and accurately to prospective student and applicant queries, ensuring a high-quality customer experience. Writing high-quality responses and overseeing those provided by enquiry assistants. Acting as a named contact for undergraduate and postgraduate applicants, delivering proactive advice and support on the progress of their applications. Liaising with academic and professional services colleagues to provide comprehensive responses to enquiries. Using the CRM system to record student details, manage enquiries, and produce regular reports on response times. Supporting and planning telephone campaigns, social media campaigns, and webinars, ensuring their successful delivery. Occasionally supervising Student Ambassadors supporting enquiry-handling work. Assisting with Open and Applicant Days, and other recruitment events, to provide advice and guidance on the admissions process. Which skills do I need? Level 3 qualifications (A levels or equivalent), with an excellent standard of written and spoken English. Experience in delivering high-quality customer service. Knowledge and understanding of the UK and/or international applicant journey. Excellent ability to work efficiently and accurately within a database or CRM system. Strong communication skills and a commitment to supporting applicants through a positive admissions experience. How to Apply If you have the vision, skills, and capabilities we are looking for, we would be delighted to hear from you. As part of the application process, please upload: Your CV A cover letter (maximum one page) that provides examples and explains how you meet the criteria outlined in the Person Specification. Selection Process: The process will include two stages: An online skills test A formal interview We encourage applicants to ensure their application reflects their own experience and skills. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. As a result of the immigration changes that came into effect from 22 July 2025 this role will not attract sufficient points to obtain a sponsored skilled worker visa under the points based immigration system, however applications are welcome from candidates who don’t currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a visa via another route. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197465 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197465 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing Recruitment & Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 07-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196746": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Senior Lecturer in Law and Technology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Associate Professor/Senior Lecturer in Law and Technology Senior Lecturer £47,389 rising annually to £58,225 Associate Professor £59,966 rising annually to £67,468 Full Time, Permanent - Academic Oxford Brookes Law School We are seeking an exceptional candidate to join our Law School as an Associate Professor or Senior Lecturer in Law and Technology. The successful candidate will play a leading role in advancing research and/or teaching on digital innovation and emerging technologies in Law and/or legal practice at a time when we are undergoing a transformation of our undergraduate and graduate teaching programmes. This post is open to both those with a research background and to those with a legal practice or teaching and learning background but with a particular expertise in Law and Technology. We are looking for a highly motivated candidate who will contribute to enhancing our student experience and employability strategy, to developing and teaching courses related to Law and Technology, and to developing our research culture or legal practice-oriented and legal skills teaching. This role would involve joining the Artificial Intelligence and Data Analytics Network (AIDAN) Committee, representing the School and strengthening connections between AIDAN and its research on the legal, ethical and regulatory dimensions of artificial intelligence and data analytics. This role will promote interdisciplinary collaboration across the University and support the development of joint research projects. Those applying with legal practice or teaching and learning experience will be working closely with our co-curricular leads to advance extensive professional networks, support students in cultivating their practice related skills, and identify opportunities for the growth and development of co-curricular activities. You will be expected to organise events and enhancement activities, as well as contribute to teaching on at least one module as outlined below. We are particularly keen to employ individuals with a working knowledge of legal tech and the use of AI in legal practice. The role offers the chance to develop and progress in the education and student experience promotion pathway as part of a highly motivated and supportive team.This post will be particularly attractive to individuals with experience of legal practice who are seeking to progress their careers in higher education, or academics with a desire to enhance their career through a focus on co-curricular activities and teaching and learning. Those applying with research experience will be required to undertake high quality personal research and other forms of scholarly activity, including seeking external funding for research and developing the impact of your research. The successful candidate will be expected to deliver engaging and high-quality teaching across a range of law modules, particularly in the area of Law and Technology, and will supervise undergraduate and postgraduate dissertations. You will provide academic guidance and support to students, and will contribute to the development of new programmes and curriculum innovations. You will also contribute to administrative duties and will be engaged in the broader academic life of the School. The successful candidate will have a record of teaching students (or evidence of an ability to teach students) across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes but particularly in the area of Computer/Digital/AI/Internet Law and/or Legal Tech. Associate Professor Applicants Candidates for the Associate Professorship role should have a PhD in Law or equivalent legal practice or academic experience; experience of initiating, developing and delivering high quality research and publications of international standing or equivalent professional activity; and experience of working effectively as part of a team to develop, manage and deliver academic programmes or equivalent professional experience. Those applying with a legal practice background will need to demonstrate an ability to teach and lead on the development of Law and Technology modules drawing on real-world professional experience to ground academic insight. Those applying with a research background will need to demonstrate a high level of engagement with research in the area of Law and Technology. Senior Lecturer Applicants Candidates applying at senior lecturer level should have a PhD or equivalent legal practice or academic experience; significant experience of teaching, mentoring, administration and leadership; and have an established record of high-quality research outputs, knowledge exchange or equivalent professional activity. This role can be applied for on a fractional basis. Interviews are planned for the week commencing 16th November 2026 . They will be in person, but can be online if needed. For more information about these roles please see the attached application information pack. If you would like to discuss any of these roles, please contact Chara Bakalis, Head of Oxford Brookes Law School, cbakalis@brookes.ac.uk If visa sponsorship is required please check your eligibility https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa How to Apply Please apply using the online application. You will need to upload: ● Your CV ● A Personal Statement, explaining how your skills and experience meet the role requirements To email the role of Associate Professor or Senior Lecturer to a friend please copy and paste the link below: https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196746 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 196746 Faculty or Directorate : Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 25-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196485": {
      "title": "Marketing Business Partner",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Marketing Business Partner £36,636 rising annually to £39,906 Full Time, Fixed Term - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Based at our John Payne Building, Gipsy Lane (with scope for hybrid working) and reporting within the Strategic Marketing & Communications team, the Marketing Business Partner will provide dedicated commercial marketing expertise within Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement (MRE) to drive income growth, occupancy, and retention across Commercial and Campus Services (Halls, Brookes Lettings, Venues, Summer Schools, Catering, and Print). This role bridges commercial objectives with the student experience, embedding the Resi Life strategy and developing data-led multi-channel growth plans to support the university's financial goals. This is a full time, fixed term role for 1 year. About the team The role sits within Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement (MRE) in collaboration with Estates and Campus Services (ECS) and Commercial and Campus Services. MRE is a confident and ambitious group of colleagues dedicated to applying professional skills and expertise to make every contact count and contribute to the University's objectives. What will I be doing? Lead and execute data-informed marketing strategies across Halls, Brookes Lettings, Venues, Summer Schools, Catering, and Print Services to directly drive income growth and achieve institutional financial targets. Elevate the Venues brand across corporate and conference markets, utilising targeted sector campaigns and digital channel optimisations to drive external bookings and year-round short-stay business. Provide strategic oversight for third-party catering marketing activities (e.g., Gather & Gather) to ensure agreed revenue targets and income contributions to the University are met. Articulate and safeguard the Commercial and Campus Services proposition across all internal and external touchpoints, ensuring high-converting digital experiences and consistent brand messaging. Manage web pages to improve conversion rates and oversee the physical positioning of the new Brookes Living shopfront in the Colonnade as a single gateway for accommodation and Resi Life. Align the Resi Life marketing strategy with university goals around student recruitment, belonging, and retention, ensuring messaging highlights inclusive provisions such as Halal and Kosher offerings. Conduct competitor benchmarking on residential pricing, incentive structures, Resi Life offerings, and digital presence to ensure competitiveness. Analyse commuting behaviors, web analytics, and enquiry data to evaluate customer demand and inform Resi Life programming, venue operations, and summer school expansion. Translate complex performance metrics and demand analysis into robust business cases to justify investments in new or repurposed university spaces (e.g., Meetings at Brookes). Utilise systems data (e.g., Kinetics) to deliver structured pipeline reporting and provide market context for strategic papers submitted to Senior Leadership and Finance Committees. What skills do I need? An appropriate degree or equivalent qualification in a marketing subject, or substantial practical experience of marketing (higher degree/professional qualification in marketing desirable). Proven experience in strategic marketing, integrated campaign delivery across digital, web, and social channels, and applying data insight to set KPIs and demonstrate ROI. Strong commercial acumen and demonstrable experience managing budgets or commercial growth strategies. Experience leading high-performing, multi-disciplinary teams and working across organisational boundaries to deliver institutional objectives. Excellent oral and written communication and stakeholder engagement skills with the ability to influence at all levels and present reports/business cases. Experience of working in the Higher Education sector, B2B operations, or commercial sectors (food and beverage, accommodation, conferencing) is desirable. A valid driving licence and ability to travel between various University sites. About the location Based primarily at our John Payne Building, Gipsy Lane, you’ll experience the vibrant campus atmosphere and benefit from our modern office environment. We encourage flexible and hybrid working where the role allows. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196485 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 196485 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 22-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197225": {
      "title": "Research Support Officer (RIE) Pre Award x2 - Internal Applicants only",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Research Support Officer (RIE) Pre Award x2 - Internal Applicants only £32,722, rising to £35,302, pro rata if part time Full Time, Fixed Term - Professional Ser PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. If you wish to apply as a secondment please speak to your line manager. Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to, a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised university focused on providing high-quality teaching and delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new, and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze Award and a Race Equality Charter Bronze Award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Based at our Headington Campus and reporting to a Research Funding Manager, the Research Support Officer (Pre-Award) will play a key role in supporting the University's research community to develop and submit high-quality research funding applications. Working within the Research Support & Governance team, you will provide expert administrative and coordination support throughout the pre-award lifecycle, advising academic staff on funder requirements, supporting proposal development and costing, and ensuring applications meet institutional and funder compliance requirements. The post-holder may also be required to contribute to a range of Faculty-aligned research support activities, working collaboratively with colleagues across the University to enable a thriving research environment. We are recruiting for two posts (1x 0.8 FTE Permanent, 1x Full-Time 3-Year Fixed Term). When applying, in the first line of your supporting statement, please specify your preference: 1) Permanent 0.8 FTE only, 2) Full-Time 3-Year Fixed Term only, or 3) Open to both. About the team The Pre Award Team sits within the Directorate of Research, Innovation and Enterprise (RIE). The Directorate supports the University's ambition to deliver world-leading research, innovation and knowledge exchange by helping researchers secure external funding, develop partnerships and maximise the impact of their work. The team works closely with academic colleagues, Faculty Research Leads, Finance teams and senior University leaders to provide professional research support across the full research lifecycle. We are a collaborative and customer-focused team, committed to delivering high-quality services that enable researchers to succeed in an increasingly competitive funding environment. What will I be doing? Supporting academic colleagues in the development, preparation and submission of high-quality research funding applications. Providing advice and guidance on funder requirements, application processes, eligibility criteria and submission requirements. Coordinating research proposals, working with internal and external collaborators to ensure bids are developed and submitted to agreed deadlines. Preparing project budgets and costings in line with funder guidance and University financial regulations, liaising with Finance and Faculty colleagues as required. Conducting detailed quality and compliance checks to ensure applications are accurate, complete and meet funder and University requirements before submission. Securing the necessary institutional approvals and submitting applications to funding bodies within required timescales. Building effective relationships with researchers and professional services colleagues to provide responsive and customer-focused research support. Maintaining up-to-date knowledge of the research funding landscape and contributing to the continuous improvement of research support processes, guidance and online resources. What skills do I need? Knowledge and understanding of higher education research support and the UK research funding landscape. Excellent organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to explain complex information clearly and effectively. Strong attention to detail and the ability to work accurately within defined policies, procedures and funding requirements. Confidence using Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, and other business systems. Ability to work collaboratively with a wide range of stakeholders, including academic staff and professional services colleagues. Proven ability to work independently, use initiative and contribute positively to team objectives. Effective problem-solving skills and a flexible approach to changing priorities and demands. About the location Based at our Headington campus, you’ll experience the vibrant campus atmosphere and benefit from our modern office environment. The campus is one mile from the centre of Oxford and is served by regular public transport. This role is hybrid and is likely to require 1 day on campus per week. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 bank holidays and additional university concessionary days (normally 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions, as well as providing all staff with access to an occupational health service, financial education, and a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the wellbeing of our employees - physically, mentally and financially - and we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the university sports and gym facilities An on-site nursery (at Headington Campus; waiting lists for some ages). Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles, subject to terms of the scheme) Training and development opportunities A connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks, which instil a sense of community and offer employees a space for support, guidance and friendship, making Brookes a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197225 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197225 Faculty or Directorate : Research, innovation and Enterprise Directorate Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.acuk Posted on : 12-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197505": {
      "title": "Senior Admissions Officer (Professional & Compliance) - Internal Applicants Only",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Senior Admissions Officer (Professional & Compliance) - Internal Applicants Only £37,369, rising to £40,704 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward-thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “We shape tomorrow through the open and inclusive exchange of knowledge and ideas” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role As Senior Admissions Officer (Professional & Compliance), you will work to ensure that applications to courses with specific professional requirements or which require additional assessment are processed in line with institutional policy and sector best practice, as well as ensuring that appropriate compliance processes are in place. You will act as the primary contact for faculty colleagues in relation to relevant programmes, providing expert advice on qualifications and market context, and conducting senior reviews of complex applications. About the team The Admissions Office sits within the Directorate of Marketing and Communications—a confident and ambitious team of colleagues who apply professional skills and expertise to make every contact count and to make a valued contribution to the University’s objectives. The Admissions Operations team delivers timely and accurate processing of admissions decisions, working closely with colleagues in faculties, agents, and partners to ensure a fair, transparent, and equitable assessment process for all applicants. What will I be doing? Provide expert advice to colleagues within the Admissions team and faculties on UK and international qualifications, market context, and professional body requirements. Act as a senior secondary reviewer for complex applications, particularly regarding professional accreditation, compliance legislation, and fee assessment legal frameworks. Line manage a dedicated team of Admissions Officers and Admissions Associates, setting clear objectives, monitoring performance, and supporting professional development. Maintain standard operating procedures and codes of practice, while delivering training and induction to team members and faculty staff involved in admissions. What skills do I need? A first degree (or equivalent professional qualification/work experience) alongside excellent written and spoken English skills. Proven experience in a higher education admissions environment, including making decisions on more complex UK and international applications and utilising database/CRM systems efficiently. Demonstrated experience in supervising or managing staff, managing workloads, and evaluating team performance and development. Strong communication, decision-making, and stakeholder management skills with the ability to act independently and influence internal and external partners effectively. About the location This role is based at Oxford Brookes University’s Headington Campus in Oxford. Headington Campus offers a vibrant and supportive working environment equipped with modern facilities, set within a historic university city known globally for educational excellence and culturally rich heritage. We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. Typically, we expect office attendance once a week, particularly for our monthly team anchor days. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous Employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197505 Closing Date : 25-Oct-2026 Vacancy ID : 197505 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment & Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 08-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197466": {
      "title": "Campus Services Support Assistant",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Campus Services Support Assistant £27,126 plus £2,712.60 roster allowance Full Time, Fixed Term - Professional Ser This is a full time (37 hours per week), 18 month contract. Oxford Brookes University is looking to recruit a reliable and highly motivated Campus Services Support Assistant as a member of the Campus Services team to undertake caretaking, cleaning and portering duties, providing exemplary facilities support services throughout the University. Campus Services Support Assistants play a proactive role within a motivated and innovative team, delivering key objectives to meet directorate and university-wide requirements. As one of the largest employers in Oxford we pride ourselves in the great experience we offer our staff. You’ll be joining a friendly, professional environment where every member of staff is recognised as important to the success of Oxford Brookes University. This is an exciting opportunity to work within the Campus Services team for our Estates & Campus Services Department. Working hours for Campus Services Support Assistant This is a full time post which is 37 hours with weekday and and weekend shifts. You will be covering 5 days out of 7 on a shift pattern (typically shifts of 07:00-14:24 and 13:36 - 21:00) The position will primarily be based at our Harcourt Hill Campus (Botley) with flexibility to support our Headington and Marston Road teams where required. Applicants who would like to have a working arrangement like this are encouraged to apply for this post. If you would like to speak to discuss this role further, please contact Campus Services Contracts Manager Delia Redding dredding@brookes.ac.uk or Sarah Warwick swarwick@brookes.ac.uk, so that arrangements can be made to hold a telephone call or video call. Overall Purpose of the Post of Campus Services Support Assistant To carry out planned, preventative and reactive Campus Services Support Assistant services across the University’s Estate, including caretaking, cleaning and portering duties, providing exemplary facilities support services. Qualifications and Experience for the post of Campus Services Support Assistant We know that sometimes people can be put off applying for a job, but we realise the 'perfect candidate' doesn't exist. So, if you are excited about working for us, go ahead and apply. You could be exactly what we need. Applicants should be able to demonstrate: ● Good written and spoken English skills ● Experience of working in a front-facing customer environment ● Exemplary customer service skills ● IT skills ● Ability to work out of normal working hours and to a designated shift pattern ● Full Driving license ● Previous experience of working unsupervised and managing own task completion. If this role looks like a good fit, we encourage you to apply early! We may close applications ahead of schedule if we receive a high response Benefits As a Campus Services Support Assistant you will also enjoy the benefits of working at Oxford Brookes University with up to 38 days holiday , rising to 41 days holiday (this includes 13 Bank Holidays and Concessionary Days), a generous Local Government pension scheme, cycle to work scheme and access to a variety of university facilities (NHS Dentist, Brookes Nursery, Gym and sports facilities). For more information about benefits, please see the document “All about Brookes” below. To apply: As part of the application process all applicants are required to complete our online application form by clicking on the “Apply for Job” button below. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. To email the post of Campus Services Support Assistant to a friend copy and paste link below https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197466 Closing Date : 01-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 197466 Faculty or Directorate : Estates and Campus Services Location : Harcourt Hill, Oxford For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 06-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196865": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Pathways",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Lecturer in Pathways £41,064, rising to £44,746 Full Time, Fixed Term - Academic Oxford Brookes Business School is looking for a Lecturer in Pathways - Could that be you? Oxford Brookes Business School is seeking to appoint an outstanding individual to the position of Lecturer (Pathways Programmes). The successful candidate will contribute to teaching across Foundation, Pre-Master’s and Pre-sessional programmes, developing students’ academic skills, English language proficiency and subject knowledge. The role will involve teaching students from diverse linguistic, cultural and educational backgrounds and contributing to curriculum development, assessment and quality assurance activities. We welcome applications from candidates with proven experience in teaching English for Academic Purposes (EAP) and delivering subject-specialist content within a Higher Education context. Experience of teaching in business-related subject areas, such as Economics or Law, would be advantageous. To find out more about this role please review the full Applicant Information Pack, which includes the job description and person specification. You can find all vacancies at Oxford Brookes Business School’s website: www.brookes.ac.uk/vacancies. The closing date is 1st November 2026. All interviews will be held online during the week beginning 15th November 2026. Candidates are usually appointed at the bottom of the salary range with a step pay increase until they reach the top of the salary scale. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 35 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 bank holidays and additional university concessionary days (normally 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions, as well as providing all staff with access to an occupational health service, financial education, and a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the wellbeing of our employees - physically, mentally and financially - and we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the university sports and gym facilities An on-site nursery (at Headington Campus; waiting lists for some ages). Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles, subject to terms of the scheme) Training and development opportunities A connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks, which instil a sense of community and offer employees a space for support, guidance and friendship, making Brookes a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196865 Closing Date : 01-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 196865 Faculty or Directorate : Oxford Brookes Business School Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-recruitment@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 29-Sep-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197205": {
      "title": "News & Media Relations Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 News & Media Relations Officer £37,369, rising to £40,704 (pro rata for part time) Part Time, Permanent - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Based at our Buckley Building on the Headington campus and reporting to the Deputy Head of Communications - News & Media Relations, the News & Media Relations Officer plays a key part in enhancing the University's visibility, reputation, and engagement through powerful digital storytelling and traditional PR. You will be responsible for creating, publishing, and evaluating multimedia content—including video, graphics, and written stories, across social, digital, and traditional media platforms, translating University achievements and research into compelling narratives that support recruitment and engage external audiences. This a part time 0.4 FTE role. About the team As part of the Directorate of Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement, the Communications team provides leadership and advice to the University on both internal and external communications. We are a confident and ambitious team dedicated to making a measurable difference to the experience of staff, prospective students, students, and alumni. Our work involves building the profile and reputation of the University amongst the media, communicating with our diverse stakeholders, and organising key events. What will I be doing? Develop proactive PR and digital communications plans to promote key areas of University activity, including teaching, research, and student experience. Plan, film, edit, and publish short-form video content optimized for platforms like Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, and YouTube. Draft media releases, expert commentary, and reactive statements to manage reputation and handle media enquiries. Identify and shape communications opportunities, working with colleagues to turn research and achievements into multi-channel storytelling outputs. Monitor performance, audience trends, and digital channels to inform content planning and improve impact. Collaborate with students, academics, and professional services teams to source content and co-create stories. Support the drafting of speeches, scripts, and editorial materials for senior staff and institutional events. What skills do I need? Degree or equivalent qualification. Proven experience in journalism, public relations, and digital communications. Demonstrated experience in proactive and reactive media relations. Strong ability to create engaging content for a wide range of platforms, including social media. Excellent oral and written communication, interpersonal, and organisational skills. (Desirable) NCTJ or CIPR (or equivalent) qualification. (Desirable) Experience of working in a charity or public sector organisation. About the location Based at our Buckley Building, Headington campus, you’ll experience a vibrant campus atmosphere and benefit from our modern office environment. The campus is one mile from the centre of Oxford and is served by regular public transport. This role will be hybrid with 1 or 2 days on campus per week. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (all leave is pro-rata for part time staff) We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous Employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting within the widest possible pool and welcome all suitably qualified applicants who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. To send this role to a friend please copy the following link: https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197205 Closing Date : 01-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 197205 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment & Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 12-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197525": {
      "title": "Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research and Innovation)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 02/11/2026 Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research and Innovation) £155,352 (national pay award pending) plus sector benefits Full Time, Permanent - Senior Staff Oxford Brookes University is seeking to appoint a Pro Vice-Chancellor (Research and Innovation) to lead the next phase of its development in research, innovation and knowledge exchange. Oxford Brookes is a distinctive university: ambitious, applied, inclusive and deeply connected to its students, staff, partners and region. It combines academic strength with a strong professional and practical orientation and has a proud history of widening opportunity and contributing to the economic, social and cultural life of Oxfordshire and beyond. Its research reflects that purpose, with 70% assessed as world-leading or internationally excellent in REF 2021. The University is now entering an important new phase. Following the appointment of a new Vice-Chancellor in 2025, Brookes has developed its Roadmap to 2030, building on the vision, mission and guiding principles of Strategy 2035. Its newly agreed research strategy sets the direction for strengthening research quality, income and impact. The appointment of a Pro Vice-Chancellor for Research and Innovation is central to delivering that ambition, making choices about priorities and investment and preparing the University for REF 2029 and beyond. Reporting to the Vice-Chancellor and working as part of the Senior Leadership Team, you will provide strategic leadership across research, innovation and knowledge exchange. You will work closely with the academic community and professional services to develop research strengths, support collaboration across disciplines and increase opportunities for external funding and commercialisation. You will also oversee the Graduate School and support the development of research staff and students, working with the Director of Research, Innovation and Enterprise to ensure that researchers have the support they need to succeed. We are looking for a senior academic leader with a strong personal record of research, funding and impact, alongside experience of improving research performance and delivering successful REF submissions. You will understand how to build an effective institutional research strategy and translate it into decisions and progress across a diverse academic community. You will bring sound judgement, a collaborative approach and the confidence to take difficult decisions while maintaining the trust and respect of colleagues. Externally, you will be an authoritative advocate for Brookes, strengthening relationships with funders, business and other partners and extending the University’s national and international research profile. For the right person, this is an opportunity to shape the next phase of research and innovation at Oxford Brookes, building on established strengths and making the most of its place within one of the world’s leading research and innovation regions. To view the candidate pack and apply please visit Anderson Quigley . Should you wish to discuss the role in strict confidence, please contact Imogen Wilde +44 (0)7511 607 522 imogen.wilde@andersonquigley.com or Ed Pritchard +44 (0)7980 817 927 ed.pritchard@andersonquigley.com The closing date for applications is noon, Monday 2 November At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197525 Closing Date : 02-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 197525 Faculty or Directorate : Vice Chancellor's Group Executive Office Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : imogen.wilde@andersonquigley.com Posted On : 07-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=196926": {
      "title": "Only for those invited - Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/12/2026 Only for those invited - Student Ambassador £16.11 per hour (includes holiday pay) Casual PLEASE DO NOT APPLY UNLESS ASKED TO BY AN ACADEMIC We are looking for enthusiastic current students to join our team of Student Ambassadors. As a student ambassador you will become part of the UK Recruitment and Partnerships team, which sits within the Directorate of Marketing Recruitment and Engagement; a confident and ambitious team of colleagues who apply professional skills and expertise to make every contact count and to make a valued contribution to the University’s objectives. UK Recruitment and Partnerships team leads on the development and delivery of high-quality recruitment events and activities designed to attract and convert a diverse pool of applicants across the University’s undergraduate and postgraduate courses. The team’s activities range from an extensive programme of school and college engagement, through to large-scale events both on-campus and virtual. Student Ambassadors are often the first point of contact a prospective student has with Oxford Brookes University; you serve as front-line staff when representing us. You are expected to provide clear and honest advice and information to all of our external customers. By acting as a positive role model you will be central in attracting applications from prospective students. You will work with students from underrepresented backgrounds, supporting them to progress to Oxford Brookes University. Your core work includes supporting the University’s seven undergraduate Open and Applicant days and 3 postgraduate evenings. You will also be able to deliver campus tours and take part in workshops and talks for schools and colleges. We're looking for motivated students who are enthusiastic about their university experience and are great at communicating that passion. You don't need any specific experience - just an awareness of what Oxford Brookes can offer and a willingness to share your experiences. We will provide you with all the training you will need. Appointment of successful candidates will be conditional on a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check which is arranged and paid for by us. Please note that if you have lived or traveled abroad for more than 3 months you will also be required to complete an overseas check before you can start work as an ambassador. You will need to undertake a Right to Work check. If you have questions about the application process or require more detail about the role, please contact: ambassadorteam@brookes.ac.uk https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=196926 Closing Date : 01-Dec-2026 Vacancy ID : 196926 Faculty or Directorate : Marketing, Recruitment and Engagement Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : ambassadorteam@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 01-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=134800": {
      "title": "Examination Invigilator",
      "description": "Examination Invigilator Various Rates Variable Hours We need to add reliable staff to our pool of invigilators for University's examinations. This role is vital to ensuring smooth running examinations and enabling our students to perform their best in every examination. We are specifically looking for those with experience in being a Chief Invigilator for a large exam room and/or Reader/Scribe Invigilators. Invigilators will undertake the following tasks: - Setting out the examination papers and supporting documents/materials in the examination room - Assisting students entering the examination room - Ensuring correct procedures and regulations are followed by students during the examination - Collecting the examination papers and supporting documents/materials at the end of the examination. There are four main examination sessions every year. However, you must be available for at least some of the dates of the May exam session. The majority of exams start at 10.00am and 14.00pm and last between one and three hours. You are able to nominate which exam dates and times you are available to work for, so it can fit in with other work or responsibilities you have. Exams take place from Monday to Saturday. Invigilators are required to arrive 1 ½ hours before the exam and are likely to finish up to one hour after the exam ends. They are able to claim an hourly rate for the whole time they are working. Invigilators must attend an invigilator training session before their first session. This role will not attract sufficient points to obtain a sponsored Skilled Worker visa under the points-based immigration system, however, applications are welcome from candidates who don’t currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a visa via another route. At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer, we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. If you are interested then please send a brief CV and the names and contact details of two referees to invigilator@brookes.ac.uk Applications are open year-round, but we have interviews only during 2 cycles between January–March and August–October. All applicants will need to be interviewed prior to appointment. To email the post of Examination Invigilator to a friend please copy and paste the link below: https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=134800 Closing Date : Vacancy ID : 134800 Faculty or Directorate : Academic and Student Administration Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted On : 30-Sep-2022"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=075222": {
      "title": "Only for those invited - Affiliate Unpaid",
      "description": "Only for those invited - Affiliate Unpaid Not Applicable Affiliate Unpaid (Unpaid Or Through E5) If you have been engaged on an Unpaid Affiliate basis, please click on the 'Apply for Job' button to complete the Unpaid Affiliate form. N.B. You are not applying for a job and will not be employed by the University. You are simply providing your personal details via this Affiliate form. N.B. Please do not click on the 'Apply for Job' button if you have not been invited to apply and asked to complete the Unpaid Affiliate form. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=075222 Closing Date : Vacancy ID : 075222 Faculty or Directorate : As advertised by recruiter Location : Across all Sites For more information : hrteam-recruitment@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 01-Jan-2020"
