    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197545": {
      "title": "Research Outputs Manager",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Research Outputs Manager £37,369 rising annually to £40,704 (pro rata if part time) Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser This is a full-time position, however part-time considered, 0.8FTE or above, preferably worked over 5 days. Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to, a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised university focused on providing high-quality teaching and delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new, and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze Award and a Race Equality Charter Bronze Award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role The Research Outputs Manager will be responsible for managing and developing Oxford Brookes’ institutional repository service. They will oversee key workflows designed to ensure that research outputs comply with University policies, funder open access mandates, requirements of the REF, and legal and ethical standards. The role will be based at our Headington campus, report to the Research & Infrastructure Lead, and collaborate closely with colleagues across the University who support researchers. About the team Part of the Directorate of Learning Resources, the Open Research Team facilitates staff and student researchers at Oxford Brookes to manage, share, and publish their research outputs. Our services cover areas such as research outputs management, open access, research data management, and compliance with policies and good practice for open research. Open Research Team members partner with colleagues and stakeholders across the Directorate and University–including the Directorate for Research, Innovation and Enterprise; research leaders; and IT Services–and participate in research committees and working groups, to help provide a supportive and connected environment for research at Oxford Brookes. What will I be doing? ● Manage and develop Oxford Brookes’ institutional repository service, including the deposit, organisation, description, preservation, and discoverability of the University’s research outputs. ● Be responsible for the management, checking, and validation of outputs uploaded via the current research information system (CRIS) and received via other submission processes. Ensure they are made open access in compliance with University policies, funder mandates, and the requirements of the latest research assessment exercise, as appropriate. ● Provide expertise in the interpretation of copyright legislation, licensing terms, and data privacy laws in relation to scholarly outputs and open access. ● Provide effective line management, set objectives, and direct the work of the Library Assistant (Open Research). ● Work collaboratively with the Research & Infrastructure Lead, Digital Infrastructure Manager, Research Data Manager, and Open Research Librarians to agree shared objectives for the delivery of a fully integrated research support service. ● Monitor developments in institutional repositories, open research services, and research infrastructure, assessing their potential to enhance services for researchers. What skills do I need? ● Experience of supporting academics and / or researchers with managing research outputs. ● Experience of supporting open research policy and practice. ● Experience of working with a research repository and / or CRIS. ● Demonstrable knowledge of the scholarly publishing landscape, including metadata standards, persistent identifiers, and relevant tools and protocols. ● Understanding of copyright, licensing, and data privacy in relation to open research. ● Able to explore more complex problems and develop solutions – thinking about causes and effects, generating options, and evaluating those options. ● Able to meet operational plans with clear targets and objectives, informed by own and others’ skills and capabilities. About the location This role is based at our Headington campus, one mile outside Oxford city centre with regular public transport links. You'll benefit from working as part of a collaborative team whilst also having flexibility through hybrid working, with regular campus attendance. For further information or to have an informal discussion about the role, please contact Katy McNeill, Research & Infrastructure Lead, at k.mcneill@brookes.ac.uk. Interviews are expected to take place on Wednesday 25 November at the Headington campus Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 bank holidays and additional university concessionary days (normally 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions, as well as providing all staff with access to an occupational health service, financial education, and a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the wellbeing of our employees - physically, mentally and financially - and we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: ● Discounted rates for the university sports and gym facilities ● An on-site nursery (at Headington Campus; waiting lists for some ages). ● Discounted travel options ● TOTUM card discount scheme ● Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles, subject to terms of the scheme) ● Training and development opportunities ● A connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks, which instil a sense of community and offer employees a space for support, guidance and friendship, making Brookes a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. To email the role of Research Outputs Manager to a friend please copy and paste the link below: https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197545 Closing Date : 08-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 197545 Faculty or Directorate : Learning Resources Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 14-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=198125": {
      "title": "Receptionist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Receptionist £14.44 per hour Variable Hours Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. This is a variable hours post, working full-time hours (Monday-Friday) during term time only from October 2026 - May 2027. About the role You will be working in the Centre for Student Development, which is a central hub that students visit to engage with services offered by colleagues working in careers and employability and academic skills development. This is a campus-based job in which you will be the first point of contact for student accessing a range of services. What you will be doing Offering a point of sensitive, inclusive and warm welcome to students visiting the Centre for Student Development Organising appointments for students visiting a range of services. Communicating with students in person and via email in a sensitive and personalised way Referring students to a range of services Prioritising and responding to incoming communications and distributing them, where appropriate to relevant staff Ensuring that confidential student records are completed accurately and fully Assisting in the cleaning of data for monitoring and evaluation purposes. What you need Experience of working in a reception or other customer service environment Ability to create a welcoming front-of-house experience Ability to communicate sensitively and accurately in person and in writing Organisation skills: good time management and attention to detail Ability to deal with students with confidential or stressful issues Flexibility and adaptability in managing a varied workload in a fast-changing environment. This role will not attract sufficient points to obtain a sponsored Skilled Worker visa under the points-based immigration system, however applications are welcome from candidates who don’t currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a visa via another route. About the location This is a customer-facing role on the Headington campus, requiring the postholder to be on campus every day, Monday to Friday. Why Join Us? At Oxford Brookes University, our people are at the heart of everything we do. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous Employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees - both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer, we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=198125 Closing Date : 01-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 198125 Faculty or Directorate : Academic and Student Administration Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 23-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197905": {
      "title": "Student Funding Administrator x2",
      "description": "Closing Date: 04/11/2026 Student Funding Administrator x2 £29,354 rising to £31,861 Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward-thinking institution rooted in and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Based at our Headington Campus (with hybrid working options), the Student Funding Administrator reports directly to the Funding Team Leader. We are currently recruiting for both permanent and fixed-term (1-year maternity cover) positions. Working closely with the Student Loans Company (SLC) and internal Registry teams, you will serve as a key point of contact for students and staff regarding tuition fee data, SLC funding, and the OBU Bursary scheme. Your duties will include ensuring data integrity across our systems (Banner and SIS), investigating and resolving discrepancies to facilitate timely payments, and managing student fee categories and waivers. You will also play a key role in supporting our students during enrollment periods and Open Days, providing a high standard of customer care across all communications. About the team The Student Finance team sits within the Finance and Legal Services (FLS) Directorate, which is central to maintaining the University’s financial integrity, operational stability, and statutory compliance. Our department is responsible for the accurate charging, collection, and allocation of tuition fees, as well as the administration of the OBU Bursary scheme. We are committed to delivering a high-quality, student-focused service. Our work involves complex data management, including maintaining data integrity between the University’s Student Record System (Banner) and the Student Loans Company (SLC) database. What will I be doing? The role involves working as part of a team to administer all aspects of financial enrolment of students with UK tuition fee and maintenance loans Completing Student Loans Company (SLC) enrolment confirmations on the SLC database to ensure that enrolled students with completed applications receive maintenance loans in a timely fashion Ensuring accurate attendance confirmation data is compiled for the SLC to allow tuition fee income to be disbursed to the University Responding to queries from applicants and students by email and telephone and updating student records with notes Offering advice on financial implications of adjustments to study patterns Responsible for investigating differences between SLC and OBU tuition fee data and resolving queries and differences to ensure correct payments. What skills do I need? Degree or equivalent Customer service experience Data input/interpretation skills Excellent communication and customer service skills Strong attention to detail Ability to work with minimal supervision. Interviews are expected to take place, in person, on 17 November 2026. Please Note: This role will not attract sufficient points to obtain a sponsored skilled worker visa under the points based immigration system, however applications are welcome from candidates who don’t currently have the right to work in the UK, but who would be eligible to obtain a visa via another route. About the location This role is hybrid, allowing for a balance between home and office working. We anticipate this role will require 1–2 days on campus per week to facilitate team collaboration and support our student-facing services. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197905 Closing Date : 04-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 197905 Faculty or Directorate : Finance and Legal Services Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.acuk Posted on : 21-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=197966": {
      "title": "Programme Director for Nursing Swindon and Nursing Associates",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Programme Director for Nursing Swindon and Nursing Associates £61,165 rising to £68,817 Full Time, Permanent - Senior Staff We are looking for a motivated individual to lead our Swindon nursing programme academic team and nursing associates across Swindon and Oxford. We are open to applications from nursing registrants. This is a full-time role of 1.0 FTE. Overall purpose of post : To lead the delivery of higher education in the areas of Nursing and Nursing Associates. To undertake academic and academic-related responsibilities, including module leadership to preregistration students. Delivering teaching and learning activities and assessments, and supervising dissertations. Qualifications required : Registered health care professional (NMC); MSc in healthcare related subject or equivalent); Teaching qualification. Experience required for post : Teaching experience of delivering pre-registration healthcare education in a higher education institution; Leadership of teams and line management; Experience of curriculum design and development. For informal enquiries about these posts please contact Dr Laura Strumidlo, Head of the Oxford School of Nursing and Midwifery lstrumidlo@brookes.ac.uk Interviews are expected to take place the week commencing 16th November 2026 As one of the largest employers in Oxford we pride ourselves in the great experience we offer our staff. You’ll be joining a friendly, professional environment where every member of staff is recognised as important to the success of Oxford Brookes University. To find out more about the benefits of working for Oxford Brookes please visit: www.brookes.ac.uk/job-vacancies/working-at-brookes. At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer, we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. To email the role of Programme Director Nursing Swindon and Nursing Associates Swindon/Oxford to a friend please copy and paste the link below: https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=197966 Closing Date : 08-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 197966 Faculty or Directorate : Health, Science and Technology Location : Swindon - Joel Joffe Building For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 19-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=198145": {
      "title": "Senior Data Analyst - Internal Applicants only",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Senior Data Analyst - Internal Applicants only £37,369 rising to £40,704, pro rata if part time Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. If you wish to apply as a secondment please speak to your line manager. Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to, a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised university focused on providing high-quality teaching and delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new, and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze Award and a Race Equality Charter Bronze Award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Based at our Headington campus and reporting to the Performance Analysis and Modelling Manager, the Senior Data Analyst will be responsible for producing high-quality analysis that will directly inform activity related to improving equality of opportunity for underrepresented groups to access, succeed in and progress from higher education. The post holder will work closely with the Performance Analysis and Modelling Manager to support the production of analysis and management information that informs senior decision‑making and supports the University’s strategic objectives. We are seeking a skilled analyst with a strong background in statistics and the analysis and reporting of data, and with an ability to effectively communicate findings and make recommendations to a range of stakeholders. Experience of working in higher education, particularly in relation to access and participation datasets would be advantageous but not essential. The post is available immediately. It is a full-time post but can also be offered part-time at no less than 0.8 FTE. About the team You will join the Modelling, Analysis and Resource Planning team within Strategic Change and Planning, part of the Academic and Student Administration Directorate. The team is responsible for reporting, analysing, forecasting and modelling a wide range of data relating to student numbers, outcomes and associated metrics. The wider division provides impartial evidence, analysis and planning expertise to support strategic decision‑making and change across the University, spanning business intelligence and analytics, modelling and forecasting, market intelligence, strategic planning, statutory returns and oversight of strategic change initiatives. The immediate team is small, supportive and enthusiastic, and you can expect to receive training, mentoring and opportunities for professional development. What will I be doing? Analyse student data and trends to help the University understand how underrepresented groups access, experience and succeed in higher education, identifying opportunities for improvement. Produce reports, insights and forecasts that support decision-making and help shape activities to improve student recruitment, success and progression. Provide expert advice on performance measures and sector developments , helping colleagues understand key metrics, benchmarks and policy changes related to access and participation. What skills do I need? Degree or equivalent in a subject with numerical and analytical content. Substantial experience of a wide range of advanced quantitative data analysis and of using statistical and other modelling techniques; including handling and interpreting complex datasets. Proven experience of presenting results, drawing conclusions and making recommendations. Experience of managing ad hoc projects. Evidence of ability to undertake statistical analysis, facilitate its interpretation and enable others to understand its implications and relevance Strong, clear and concise written and verbal communication skills. Excellent communication and presentation skills, both written and verbal, and the ability to convey complex information to non-experts. Excellent IT skills, with particular emphasis on statistics, spreadsheet packages and presentations e.g. SPSS, advanced Excel and PowerPoint. Accuracy and attention to detail. Strong self-organisation skills, including the ability to handle several projects simultaneously. About the location Based at our Headington campus , you’ll experience the vibrant campus atmosphere and benefit from our modern office environment. The campus is one mile from the centre of Oxford and is served by regular public transport. The role will be hybrid and we expect this role is likely to require 1-2 days on campus per week. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 25 days holiday, rising with your service, plus 8 bank holidays and additional university concessionary days (normally 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions, as well as providing all staff with access to an occupational health service, financial education, and a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the wellbeing of our employees - physically, mentally and financially - and we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the university sports and gym facilities An on-site nursery (at Headington Campus; waiting lists for some ages) Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles, subject to terms of the scheme) Training and development opportunities A connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks, which instil a sense of community and offer employees a space for support, guidance and friendship, making Brookes a vibrant and inclusive place to work. Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=198145 Closing Date : 08-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 198145 Faculty or Directorate : Academic and Student Administration Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 26-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=198245": {
      "title": "Information Governance Officer - Internal Applicants Only",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Information Governance Officer - Internal Applicants Only £37,369, rising to £40,704 (Pro-rata for part time) Full Time, Permanent - Professional Ser PLEASE NOTE: This is an internal advert and is open to current Oxford Brookes University staff only. At Oxford Brookes University, we take immense pride in the outstanding experience we offer our staff. You’ll become part of a welcoming, professional community where every individual is valued and recognised as integral to our collective success. As a modern, forward-thinking institution, we are deeply rooted in a city renowned for its rich cultural and academic heritage. Oxford Brookes is globally recognised for its commitment to high-quality teaching, impactful research, and delivering an exceptional student experience. Our vision is clear: to shape tomorrow through a unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking innovation, and excelling in education and research. About the Role We are seeking an Information Governance Officer (IGO) with specialist knowledge and experience to join our Information Assurance and Compliance team. This is a full-time post but can also be offered part-time at no less than 0.8 FTE. As a key member of the team, you will independently manage and develop a defined information-governance portfolio, providing specialist advice on complex, sensitive and non-routine matters across the University. You will support the University in meeting its statutory, regulatory and contractual obligations through specialist advice, complex casework, assurance and improvement activity. Your managed portfolio will include data protection, privacy and information rights under the UK GDPR, Data Protection Act 2018 and Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations 2003 (PECR), including relevant changes introduced by the Data (Use and Access) Act 2025, alongside the Freedom of Information Act 2000 and Environmental Information Regulations 2004. You will also advise on the information-governance implications of AI, including relevant requirements of the EU AI Act and others where applicable. You will provide practical advice on procurement, suppliers, contracts, research, data sharing and international transfers. You will manage assigned information-rights casework, coordinate the information-governance response to assigned incidents, lead assigned projects and improvement work, and contribute to assurance reviews, guidance and training. Knowledge of relevant information-security and privacy standards, including ISO 27001, ISO 42001 would be advantageous, as would familiarity with the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS). About You You will combine independent specialist judgement with a collaborative approach, working effectively with academic and professional-service colleagues, technical specialists, legal advisers and suppliers. You will take ownership of complex matters, manage competing priorities and recognise when further advice, authorisation or escalation is required. You will bring: Substantial specialist experience in the field of information governance, data protection and/or information security within a complex landscape. Ability to interpret and apply complex legislation, regulatory guidance and professional standards independently. Experience of managing complex, sensitive or high-risk matters and translating legal, regulatory and risk requirements into clear advice and practical recommendations. Experience of managing a workload of compliance, assurance or improvement projects or activities. If this opportunity appeals and you meet all or most of the requirements, we strongly encourage you to apply. Working Arrangements We support hybrid working. While our team is based at the Headington Campus in Oxford, we are happy to explore flexible arrangements that balance remote work with time spent on campus to foster team engagement and collaboration. There is an expectation to be on campus at least one day per week. About the Location Our vibrant Headington campus is just one mile from the centre of Oxford and is easily accessible by regular public transport. You’ll enjoy the lively atmosphere and the opportunity to be part of a thriving academic community. How to Apply To apply, please complete our online application form by clicking the “Apply for Job” button below. In the “Supporting Documents” section, please upload your CV and a cover letter detailing how you meet the person-specification. Equality, Diversity and Inclusion Inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles at Oxford Brookes. We are committed to creating an environment where everyone is celebrated, valued, and given equal opportunities. We encourage applications from all suitably qualified candidates who share our values, regardless of background. For an informal discussion with a recruiting manager, please contact ITS/ASA Operations team, its-asaoperations@brookes.ac.uk. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=198245 Closing Date : 15-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 198245 Faculty or Directorate : IT Services Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 27-Oct-2026"
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=198246": {
      "title": "Head of Data and Integrations",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/11/2026 Head of Data and Integrations £72,997, rising to £79,750 (Pro rata for part time) Full Time, Permanent - Senior Staff Oxford Brookes University is distinctive in nature. We are a modern and forward thinking institution rooted in, and connected to a city with a rich history of culture and learning. We are a globally recognised University focused on providing high-quality teaching, delivering impactful research and an excellent student experience. Our vision is simple: “shape tomorrow through our unique blend of the modern and the traditional, by embracing diversity, seeking out the new and excelling in education and research.” Our people are at the heart of the University - our excellence in teaching, research and knowledge exchange depends on the engagement, capability and wellbeing of our people. We strive to create and encourage an environment where people have the opportunity to develop, progress and thrive. In acknowledgment of our commitment to gender equality and progression, we proudly hold the Athena SWAN Bronze award, a testament to our unwavering dedication to creating an inclusive and equitable environment for all. Join us at Oxford Brookes University, where every step forward is a leap toward a brighter tomorrow. The role Are you an experienced and visionary software and data expert ready to lead with new and innovative ways of working? Do you thrive on transforming ambitious strategies into rock solid and cutting edge solutions? Then join us and take the helm as our Head of Data and Integrations! This isn't just a management job, it's your chance to be the strategic architect of the people, technology, and processes that power a leading university's entire Digital Strategy and future outlook. We're looking for a senior leader to define, deliver, and manage a robust development, data, and integrations strategy spanning campus solutions, partners, and our expanding cloud services. This is a full-time post but can also be offered part-time at no less than 0.8 FTE. What You'll Be Doing You will be the driving force behind our technical evolution when it comes to development, data, and integrations, directly impacting world class learning, teaching excellence, research, and innovation. Strategic Visionary: You’ll be at the forefront of tech, investigating and piloting new technologies to identify opportunities for competitive advantage and deliver enhanced student experiences. Modern Pipeline & Integrations Pioneer: You’ll lead on building a modern integrations approach and development pipeline that leverages AI and automation technologies to increase efficiency, quality, and security. Data Expert: You’ll lead and drive effective data architecture and governance to inform strategic decisions and support operational excellence across the University. Relationship Builder: You’ll forge effective relationships across the University and with key external partners to ensure our technology supports all organisational needs, including robust measures for business continuity and disaster recovery. Risk & Prioritisation: You’ll develop forward looking strategic and development plans, skillfully prioritising initiatives and conducting comprehensive risk assessments. About the team IT Services at Oxford Brookes University is a modern, service-oriented environment that is constantly embracing change. You will be joining the team at an exciting time and will be contributing to the Digital Strategy which aims to transform university life through the use of digital technologies and services, as well as delivering excellent customer service. In return you will be provided with development opportunities both professionally and personally that will enable you to continue to enhance your skills and knowledge. About the location This role is based on a Hybrid working model, with the primary base being the Headington Campus. Benefits As an Oxford Brookes employee, you will enjoy a total of a minimum of 30 days holiday, plus 8 Bank Holidays and additional University concessionary Days (approx 5 per year). We encourage and support hybrid working where the role allows and ensure that you have the necessary equipment to allow you to work flexibly. We have an extremely competitive Local Government pension scheme with a generous Employer contribution rate, as well as providing all staff with financial education, a comprehensive employee assistance helpline. We prioritise the well-being of our employees—both physically and mentally, as well as financially. That's why we provide a diverse and comprehensive benefits package to support our team. In addition, all employees have access to: Discounted rates for the University sports & gym facilities Brookes on-site Nursery. Discounted travel options TOTUM card discount scheme Relocation scheme (for moves over 30 miles) Training and development opportunities Connected community - Brookes have a wide variety of staff networks which instil a sense of community offering employees a space for support, guidance and friendship making it a vibrant and inclusive place to work Equality, diversity and inclusion At Oxford Brookes, inclusivity is one of our five guiding principles: we take positive steps to create an environment in which we celebrate, value and provide equal opportunity to all. We are committed to recruiting from the widest possible pool and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates who embrace our values, regardless of their background. As a Disability Confident Employer we guarantee to interview any disabled applicant who meets the essential selection criteria. For an informal discussion with a recruiting manager please ITS/ASA Operations team, its-asaoperations@brookes.ac.uk. https://my.corehr.com/pls/oburecruit/erq_jobspec_details_form.jobspec?p_id=198246 Closing Date : 22-Nov-2026 Vacancy ID : 198246 Faculty or Directorate : IT Services Location : Gipsy Lane Site, Headington Campus For more information : pdteam-operations@brookes.ac.uk Posted on : 27-Oct-2026"
    }
  },
